{
 "_comment": [
  "Conformance vectors for the register document schemas.",
  "",
  "schema.valid must pass the schema. schema.invalid must fail it.",
  "",
  "schema.semantic is the third kind and the important one. Each must PASS the",
  "schema and fail only in the validator. A schema cannot express a rule that",
  "spans two fields, so trying to make it do so grows a rule it should not have.",
  "hack/validate.sh asserts both halves, which is what stops that.",
  "",
  "The get, put and list transport is owned by forge-revision-spec and its",
  "vectors live there. Register records are new kinds over that transport, so",
  "there is nothing transport shaped to assert here."
 ],
